    'getting_started_partner_purpose' => 'This chapter helps dealers and sub-dealers log in safely to their own panel and get ready for daily work.',
    'getting_started_partner_s1' => 'Know your login page: dealer — dealer, sub-dealer — subdealer. The public website is only for browsing.',
    'getting_started_partner_s8' => 'Bookmark only your own panel\'s address, so you always open the right login page.',
    'getting_started_partner_s9' => 'If login fails, check the panel address, your login details, and whether your account is active or suspended.',
    'getting_started_partner_why' => 'Logging in to the wrong panel will not work. Starting at the right address avoids blocked logins and missing sections.',
    'catalog_orders_s13' => 'When you order, choose how to pay: by bKash, Nagad, Rocket or bank with proof; By Office (cash at the office, and the office confirms when it gets the money); or From My Account (taken from the money you can use now, and the order cannot cost more than that).',
    'inventory_branches_s12' => 'Goods that leave for delivery are no longer counted in stock. They show as With courier until they are delivered. If they are not delivered and come back, they go back into stock.',
    'settings_home_badge' => 'Settings',
    'settings_home_title' => 'The Settings page: what each link is for',
    'settings_home_summary' => 'One page of links for company rules and connections. You see only the links you can open.',
    'settings_home_purpose' => 'Rarely used pages are together on Settings, so they stay out of the way of daily work.',
    'settings_home_why' => 'A setting changes how the whole system works, so know what a link does before you change anything.',
    'settings_home_s1' => 'Account rules: switches for how partners pay and get paid. With full payment on, a partner can send an order only with the whole payment and its screenshot. With the ID rule on, a partner cannot ask for a first withdrawal until the office has saved their ID papers. With automatic payment on, a dealer who meets the rules is paid with nobody approving it, so turn it off when you have staff to check each payment.',
    'settings_home_s2' => 'bKash and bank numbers: the company accounts partners pay into.',
    'settings_home_s3' => 'Check opening balances: old balances are checked here before live money records start. A fresh start needs no Excel file and no old balances. Neither choice turns on live money records by itself.',
    'settings_home_s4' => 'Area codes: the place codes for each division, district, upazila and union.',
    'settings_home_s5' => 'Partner panels: turn parts of the dealer and sub-dealer panels on or off, show a notice at the top of every page, or close a panel for a while during maintenance. Staff can keep working.',
    'settings_home_s6' => 'Same person, two accounts: accounts that may belong to one person because the NID or phone matches.',
    'settings_home_s7' => 'Login and password rules: the SMS code at sign-in. An account with no mobile number cannot sign in while this is on, so turn it off only if the SMS service is down. When a staff member who is not an owner resets a password, every owner gets a notice. The notice never shows the new password. Reason and note boxes: which forms must have a reason or note, which may leave it blank, and which do not ask at all. Nothing is compulsory for the owner\'s own account.',
    'settings_home_s8' => 'SMS and courier connections: these services stay off until you turn them on and enter the login details. Work done by hand carries on without them.',
    'settings_home_s9' => 'Courier areas: which areas each courier delivers to.',
